            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_0",
            "review_title": "Review at Song Trang Restaurant",
            "review_text": "R K L\nSeattle, Washington4203 contributions\n0\nA favorite of locals and entrance was easy to miss...\nJan 2020\nThe dining experience was luckily very nice but would have been substantially different if the restaurant known as Moon River had firstly not been suggested by our hotel, and secondly, if we had not gone with a local friend. Our hotel suggested and made advance reservations, so when we arrived to a very large, chaotic and packed Song Trang, we were pleased when shown to a more secluded, quiet table overlooking the river. Since little to no English was spoken by the staff, being there with our Vietnamese friend was a must. The restaurant is supposedly a favorite of locals and frequently hosts large groups and family celebrations. Since our visit was on a Friday night at the start of the Lunar New Year weekend, the restaurant had a wonderfully festive, electric atmosphere. Although we had received specific directions from our hotel to the restaurant, the entrance was easy to miss. We actually walked by several times. The meal we ordered was the equivalent of a family-style banquet and was excellent. With drinks and desserts, the total cost for the four of us was a whopping $32 USD! And the servers, even though harried, were extremely friendly, professional and responsive. Tipping was supposedly not expected but clearly appreciated. Now comparing all of the above dining experience to most anywhere in the USA, is there something wrong with the picture?\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 3, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
