            "review_title": "Review at Song Trang Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Sally\nBristol, United Kingdom282 contributions\n0\nLocal restaurant in riverside setting\nApr 2017\nAte here on the recommendation of Saigon Domain where we were staying. Enjoyed it so much that we returned every evening of our stay at the hotel.\nRestaurant is located in a quiet setting with outside tables ohverlooking the river. It is a local restaurant selling local food with a couple of western options. The menu is extensive containing enough English and pictures to help you choose your dishes. The waiters were friendly and spoke adequate English to understand your order and requests for drinks etc. We found there was plenty of variety and chose different dishes most evenings. Would say that the local food, (as usual everywhere), was better, always hot, fresh and tasty. All prices, including the local beer served in cans, were very cheap. The atmosphere was friendly and welcoming. Always busy with local people, especially families, who seemed to eat here for special occasions. One evening we ordered the roll your own spring rolls by mistake and when the dish arrived we did not have a clue what to do. Whilst sitting there looking confused another diner, who was local but spoke excellent English, asked us if we needed help and proceeded to show us exactly how to roll the pancakes. They were, by the way, delicious. \nWe found this local friendly restaurant to serve better food at a cheaper price than any restaurant we tried in the city centre and would definitely recommend eating here especially if staying locally.\nRead more\nWritten October 21, 2017",
