            "review_title": "Review at Song Trang Restaurant",
            "review_text": "4Ellis\nNew York City, New York41 contributions\n0\nClose to the hotel. OK food\nAug 2017 • Couples\nWe walked down the road from our hotel to the restaurant. We were seated promptly and given a menu with many pictures. The place was sort of empty when we arrived but it started to fill up quickly with some very large groups and also some couples. There was plenty of room for everybody. The restaurant had a happy buzz.\n\nThe two of us ordered 1 appetizer, a noodle dish, and a seafood dish. The picture of the appetizer showed only pork but it came with noodles and a mixture of fresh greens and herbs. Nice. The Saigon noodles were described as vegetarian but to my surprise there was sliced pork in it. Not a deal breaker for me but it might be for others. I did not eat the seafood dish but my partner seemed to like it fine. We had lots of leftovers which were packed up for us and we had them for dinner the next day.\nRead more\nWritten August 27, 2017",
