            "review_text": "Dominic_Jaar\nMontreal, Canada43 contributions\n0\nGood neighboorhoud food, but no english speaking staff member\nJan 2017 • Family\nThis restaurant was an easily accessible location if you happen to be around but does not justify anyone going out of their way. The food was good at a reasonable price. The only bad thing, as a tourist, is that no one spoke english (or french - and I assume any other language, except Vietnamese) which created problems for us since I have an allergic son and the staff didn't understand what it meant and the implications... For example, after trying really hard to explain that my son can't eat peanuts and tree nuts, the waiter came with a nice piece of beef, with peanut chunks on it. My boy ended up having rice and a Coca-Cola, with non-purified ice.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten January 18, 2017",
